Use gmtime_r, because gmtime shares one static buffer between all threads.

The 2.36 form of `nix-gmtime-not-thread-safe.patch`. The defect and the repair
are the same, and the patch header of that file gives the ThreadSanitizer
report and the reasoning. Read it first.

Only the context differs. `emitTreeAttrs` in `src/libexpr/primops/fetchTree.cc`
gained a `callPos` argument on the default branch, so the hunk of the released
form does not apply. `src/libflake/lockfile.cc` is unchanged, and its hunk is
the same in both files.

**This is still needed on the default branch.** Both call sites of `std::gmtime`
are still there at adee4313, so nothing upstream has repaired this yet. Check
before deleting: `grep -rn gmtime src/libexpr/primops/fetchTree.cc
src/libflake/lockfile.cc`.

This is nanopynix issue #90.

diff -ruN a/src/libexpr/primops/fetchTree.cc b/src/libexpr/primops/fetchTree.cc
--- a/src/libexpr/primops/fetchTree.cc	2026-08-08 17:49:50.641640033 +0200
+++ b/src/libexpr/primops/fetchTree.cc	2026-08-08 17:49:50.683464001 +0200
@@ -167,8 +167,11 @@
 
     if (auto lastModified = input.getLastModified()) {
         attrs.alloc("lastModified", callPos).mkInt(*lastModified);
+        // See the comment in libflake/lockfile.cc's describe(): gmtime shares
+        // one static buffer between every thread, and gmtime_r does not.
+        struct tm tmBuf;
         attrs.alloc("lastModifiedDate", callPos)
-            .mkString(fmt("%s", std::put_time(std::gmtime(&*lastModified), "%Y%m%d%H%M%S")), state.mem);
+            .mkString(fmt("%s", std::put_time(::gmtime_r(&*lastModified, &tmBuf), "%Y%m%d%H%M%S")), state.mem);
     }
 
     v.mkAttrs(attrs);
diff -ruN a/src/libflake/lockfile.cc b/src/libflake/lockfile.cc
--- a/src/libflake/lockfile.cc	2026-08-08 17:49:50.642640028 +0200
+++ b/src/libflake/lockfile.cc	2026-08-08 17:49:50.684619732 +0200
@@ -349,8 +349,14 @@
 {
     auto s = fmt("'%s'", flakeRef.to_string());
 
-    if (auto lastModified = flakeRef.input.getLastModified())
-        s += fmt(" (%s)", std::put_time(std::gmtime(&*lastModified), "%Y-%m-%d"));
+    if (auto lastModified = flakeRef.input.getLastModified()) {
+        // gmtime writes one static buffer that every thread shares, so two
+        // evaluator threads formatting a lastModified corrupt each other's
+        // result. gmtime_r writes the caller's buffer and returns it, which
+        // keeps this a single expression.
+        struct tm tmBuf;
+        s += fmt(" (%s)", std::put_time(::gmtime_r(&*lastModified, &tmBuf), "%Y-%m-%d"));
+    }
 
     return s;
 }
